  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be maintained in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r\rLocation Plan  - MX500185\rBlock Plan - TQRQM25194191238995\rExisting Retrospective Floor Plans-  218/02\rExisting Retrospective Elevations and Section Plans-  218/03\r\rHighways proforma\r\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen/living room shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Within 2 months of this permission, details of the siting, number and design of cycle parking spaces preferably at the frontage shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details maintained as such thereafter. \r\rReason: To ensure the provision of cycle parking in line with the Council's adopted standards\r",
    "Within 2 months of this permission, details of refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste to be provided within the development, in accordance with the London Borough of Enfield Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024), shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The facilities shall be provided in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r"
  ],
